    "title": "Oklahoma City Felon Gets 12 Years After Flock Camera Ties Him to Drive-By Shooting - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Megan Sousa ,\n8 hours ago A 43-year-old Oklahoma City man has been sentenced to 12 years in federal prison after investigators used ballistics testing and license plate camera footage to tie a gun found in his car to a drive-by shooting at an occupied home. Marree Kavon Currie was stopped by police for not wearing a seatbelt in Oklahoma City on August 22, 2025, and told officers a gun was inside his vehicle before detectives seized the weapon. Investigators later connected that same firearm to a shooting that sent multiple gunshots into a home just over a week earlier. Read full article\n1",
